# Line endings: the index already stores LF (verified with `git ls-files --eol`: 721 of 721 tracked
# files), while `core.autocrlf=true` checked the working tree out as CRLF for 507 of them and left six
# files with mixed endings — those six were exactly the files edited by append-style patches in recent
# rounds, and each one produced a whole-file diff that had to be normalised by hand before committing.
#
# `eol=lf` keeps the working tree consistent with the index on every platform, so a small edit stays a
# small diff. Nothing about the stored content changes; only the checkout.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows shells want CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binaries and generated artefacts must never be converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
*.xlsx binary
*.docx binary
*.zip binary
*.tar binary
*.gz binary
*.7z binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
*.pem binary
*.key binary
*.p12 binary
